  "independent_tests_passed": 10,
  "findings": [
    "Episode diff is limited to recovery controller selection, explicit visibility policy, per-request declared messages/tools and guarded expanded snapshot recording. Existing recycler admission, history retention, terminal selection/export and call/token budgeting paths remain.",
    "Declared toolset is fixed for each submitted request and tool batch. Staged open does not expose expanded tools until the next prepare; undeclared same-batch recovery is rejected.",
    "Recovery acknowledgement reconstructs the actual successful submitted request by receipt digest; tokenizer candidates or incomplete output do not count as successful presentation. Expanded mode validates page and freshness message; entry mode invents no archive snapshot.",
    "Controller and retained archive survive actual recycling; source becomes available only after successful request delivery, not merely tool return. Tests confirm original read identity and native export.",
    "Eight inherited regressions and two new real-recycler synthetic-transport scenarios pass, including known failed costs, admission failure, raw argument rejection and output deferral."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No provider generation, actual runtime fit, efficiency or quality evidence established by synthetic tests.",
    "Future paired protocol must state snapshot timing and exact eager/demand projection differences; unchanged controller semantics do not imply identical first-snapshot timing.",
    "Compact final reference persistence, bounded runner integration, full cumulative accounting and exact prospective freeze remain prerequisites."
  ],
